      "body": "Two people in northeastern Nigeria are suspected of having contracted the Ebola virus.\nAccording to the country's Centre for Disease Control and Prevention, both individuals, who developed fever, have been isolated, while health officials are assessing their medical condition and tracing their contacts. Ebola infection has not yet been confirmed, and laboratory test results are expected to determine whether they have contracted the virus.\nNigeria confirmed its first Ebola case on October 26. The patient was a Swiss national who had travelled to Nigeria by plane from Uganda.\nMeanwhile, the death toll from Ebola in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) has exceeded 5,000. According to the country's National Institute of Public Health, 10,351 people have been infected with the virus.\nThe outbreak began in May this year in the DRC and Uganda. In the DRC, infections and deaths have been reported in eight provinces.",
