      "body": "NAIROBI, Kenya — More than 5,000 people have died from Ebola in the Democratic Republic of the Congo since the latest outbreak of the virus was detected in mid-May, according to the country's health authorities. A total of 5,026 deaths have been confirmed, while the number of infections has risen to 10,351, the authorities said.\nAdd Spokesman-Review on Google By Eva-Maria Krafczyk German Press Agency NAIROBI, Kenya — More than 5,000 people have died from Ebola in the Democratic Republic of the Congo since the latest outbreak of the virus was detected in mid-May, according to the country’s health authorities.\nThe actual toll could be higher, as experts believe the virus may have been spreading undetected since at least February, several months before the outbreak was officially declared on May 15.",
